2026-05-20 16:21:34,320 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized agents, proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily missions. Our solution integrates AI-powered information systems, ensuring data sovereignty, GDPR compliance, and low carbon impact. We leverage our expertise in cloud architecture, cybersecurity, and digital transformation to provide an intelligent assistance tool that facilitates access to information, improves answer quality, and reduces processing times.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an artificial intelligence solution that provides assistance with consultation of information, drafting, instruction of files, and collaboration. The solution must respect regulatory requirements, including GDPR compliance, data sovereignty, and explicability of recommendations. Technical constraints include high availability, fast response times, integration with existing systems, and low carbon impact.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution utilizes the Mistral 7B Instruct large language model, an EU-origin model with strong French-language performance and self-hostable capabilities. To optimize energy usage, we apply quantisation methods such as INT8 and INT4 (GPTQ) and fine-tuning methods like LoRA and QLoRA. Our technical architecture integrates with existing business software, EDM, and user directories using API-type interfaces like REST or GraphQL. We ensure data sovereignty by hosting data exclusively on European Union territory, utilizing cloud providers like Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud, which offer high security standards.

For security and compliance, we implement measures such as anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio, custom NER models, and Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA). Our standard data residency policy ensures that data is stored within the EU only, and our cross-border transfer policy prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there is an explicit legal basis.

Our solution is designed with a high level of availability, aiming for 99.9% uptime, and fast response times, with a target of less than 2 seconds for current requests. We utilize containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) and monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana to ensure high performance.

In terms of costs, we aim to optimize expenses while maintaining quality. With a global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years, our annual cost would be approximately 750,000 euros per year. Assuming a target gross margin of 28%, our projected revenue on this contract would cover our costs and ensure a reasonable profit.

To reduce the environmental footprint, we apply digital sobriety practices like INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and green IT hardware procurement. Our partnership with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway ensures that our infrastructure relies on 100% renewable energy and has a low power usage effectiveness (PUE) ratio.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender are unaddressed in our proposal.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. and its consortium propose a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution that addresses the City of Belval's needs for an intelligent assistance tool. Our solution integrates AI-powered information systems, ensuring data sovereignty, GDPR compliance, and low carbon impact. With a focus on technical expertise, security, and sustainability, we are confident that our proposal meets the requirements and constraints outlined in the tender.
